--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
unexpected expression
--
User-reported: `template <class T> struct G { ... } __attribute__((packed,
aligned(16)));` -- "class templates must not be anonymous", then `G`
unknown everywhere.  The parser merges trailing attributes around the
class-specifier (merged_type of attribute nodes and the struct); for a
class TEMPLATE the declaration is kept as parsed, so the merged node had
no tag.  Fold the recognised attributes onto the struct as the layout
flags (N5008 [dcl.attr.grammar]/5: the attributes appertain to the
class).  Both instantiations must be 16 bytes (packed, then aligned).
